# Route Interfaces

This Livebook defines one exact route and uses its generated map-based Signal constructor.

## Install Jido

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:jido, path: Path.expand("..", __DIR__)}
])
```

## Define The Route

```elixir
defmodule RouteInterfaces.SetStatus do
  use Jido.Action,
    name: "route_interfaces_set_status",
    schema: Zoi.object(%{status: Zoi.enum([:open, :closed])})

  @impl Jido.Action
  def run(%{status: status}, %{agent_state: state}) do
    {:ok, %{state | status: status}}
  end
end

defmodule RouteInterfaces.Order do
  use Jido.Agent, name: "route_interfaces_order"

  agent do
    schema(Zoi.object(%{status: Zoi.enum([:open, :closed]) |> Zoi.default(:open)}))
  end

  routes do
    signal_source("/guides/route-interfaces")

    route "order.status.set", RouteInterfaces.SetStatus do
      define(:set_status)
    end
  end
end
```

A generated interface requires an exact route with no match predicate. This
keeps one helper tied to one executable target.

## Construct A Signal

```elixir
{:ok, signal} = RouteInterfaces.Order.set_status_signal(%{status: :closed})

%{
  type: signal.type,
  source: signal.source,
  data: signal.data
}
```

The constructor returns `{:ok, signal}` or `{:error, reason}`. It does not execute
the command.

## Add Envelope And Input Data

```elixir
{:ok, signal} =
  RouteInterfaces.Order.set_status_signal(%{status: :closed, request_id: "req-1"},
    subject: "order-7"
  )

{signal.data.request_id, signal.subject}
```

Input is one plain map. Envelope options cannot replace the Signal type or data.

## Call The Server

```elixir
{:ok, _jido} = Jido.start()

{:ok, order} =
  Jido.start_agent(
    RouteInterfaces.Order,
    id: "order-7"
  )

{:ok, committed} =
  with {:ok, signal} <- RouteInterfaces.Order.set_status_signal(%{status: :closed}) do
    Jido.AgentServer.call(order, signal, context: %{actor: "reviewer"}, timeout: 5000)
  end

committed.state.status
```

Pass runtime context and the wait timeout to `Jido.AgentServer.call/3`.

## Stop The Example

```elixir
:ok = Jido.stop_agent(order)
:ok = Jido.stop()
```

See [Signals, Commands, And Routes](signals-commands-and-routes.md) for route
selection rules.
